{"id": "wwdc2019-716", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/716", "wordCount": 1236, "segments": [{"start": 8.0, "text": "Last year in watchOS 5, we"}, {"start": 10.0, "text": "introduced the ability to play"}, {"start": 12.0, "text": "local, long-form audio in the"}, {"start": 13.0, "text": "background."}, {"start": 16.0, "text": "This year with watchOS 6, we're"}, {"start": 18.0, "text": "bringing the ability for watch"}, {"start": 19.0, "text": "apps to stream audio directly on"}, {"start": 21.0, "text": "Apple Watch."}, {"start": 23.0, "text": "This means that your customers"}, {"start": 25.0, "text": "no longer need to bring their"}, {"start": 26.0, "text": "iPhone with them to access your"}, {"start": 28.0, "text": "audio content, they no longer"}, {"start": 30.0, "text": "need to sync audio content to"}, {"start": 31.0, "text": "their watches, and they now have"}, {"start": 33.0, "text": "access to live audio programing"}, {"start": 35.0, "text": "like sports events."}, {"start": 37.0, "text": "WatchOS 6 supports two main ways"}, {"start": 40.0, "text": "to stream audio to Apple Watch."}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "HLS and custom audio protocols."}, {"start": 47.0, "text": "Let's dive into a bit more"}, {"start": 50.0, "text": "detail."}, {"start": 51.0, "text": "If your content is available as"}, {"start": 53.0, "text": "an HLS audio feed, you can point"}, {"start": 56.0, "text": "AVQueuePlayer to the feed and it"}, {"start": 58.0, "text": "will take care of streaming your"}, {"start": 59.0, "text": "content."}, {"start": 61.0, "text": "WatchOS is optimized for HLS"}, {"start": 63.0, "text": "audio feeds and makes it simple"}, {"start": 65.0, "text": "to get started with."}, {"start": 67.0, "text": "Applications that use"}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "proprietary audio formats or use"}, {"start": 71.0, "text": "custom protocols are a bit"}, {"start": 72.0, "text": "different."}, {"start": 74.0, "text": "They need to use URLSession on"}, {"start": 77.0, "text": "the network framework to"}, {"start": 78.0, "text": "retrieve and interpret their"}, {"start": 80.0, "text": "metadata and audio content."}, {"start": 83.0, "text": "Once audio content has been"}, {"start": 85.0, "text": "downloaded to the watch, use"}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "AVFoundation for audio route"}, {"start": 88.0, "text": "selection and audio playback."}, {"start": 93.0, "text": "Audio streaming is made possible"}, {"start": 94.0, "text": "in watchOS 6 by bringing several"}, {"start": 96.0, "text": "iOS APIs into the watchOS SDK."}, {"start": 99.0, "text": "Our goal has been to bring the"}, {"start": 101.0, "text": "two SDKs closer together so that"}, {"start": 103.0, "text": "your code can run watchOS with"}, {"start": 105.0, "text": "little or no modification."}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "For networking, watchOS 6 now"}, {"start": 111.0, "text": "has the network framework, first"}, {"start": 113.0, "text": "introducing iOS 12."}, {"start": 115.0, "text": "This framework provides a modern"}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "alternative to unit sockets."}, {"start": 118.0, "text": "Network framework is not only"}, {"start": 120.0, "text": "more on C API but also provides"}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "a very convenient Swift API."}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "URLSession brings"}, {"start": 127.0, "text": "URLSessionStreamingTask to"}, {"start": 129.0, "text": "watchOS."}, {"start": 130.0, "text": "It also brings along"}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "URLSessionWebSocketTask, which"}, {"start": 134.0, "text": "is new in both iOS 13 and in"}, {"start": 136.0, "text": "watchOS 6."}, {"start": 138.0, "text": "Audio streaming presents special"}, {"start": 139.0, "text": "challenges to the way the data"}, {"start": 141.0, "text": "is retrieved from the network."}, {"start": 143.0, "text": "To this end, URLSession has"}, {"start": 145.0, "text": "added the new AV streaming"}, {"start": 147.0, "text": "network service type."}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "You should use it for your"}, {"start": 149.0, "text": "streaming data request."}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "For audio playback, AVFoundation"}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "is bringing many of their APIs"}, {"start": 155.0, "text": "to watchOS 6 including AVPlayer"}, {"start": 159.0, "text": "and AVQueuePlayer."}, {"start": 162.0, "text": "Also, for the first time,"}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "CoreMedia is available in"}, {"start": 165.0, "text": "watchOS."}, {"start": 167.0, "text": "If your application is already"}, {"start": 168.0, "text": "set up for background audio"}, {"start": 170.0, "text": "playback, it is ready for audio"}, {"start": 172.0, "text": "streaming."}, {"start": 173.0, "text": "No other project configuration"}, {"start": 174.0, "text": "is needed."}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "If your project is not"}, {"start": 177.0, "text": "configured for background audio,"}, {"start": 178.0, "text": "you will need to add this"}, {"start": 180.0, "text": "capability to the WatchKit"}, {"start": 181.0, "text": "extension target."}, {"start": 183.0, "text": "For this, open your Xcode"}, {"start": 185.0, "text": "project and go to your WatchKit"}, {"start": 186.0, "text": "extension target settings."}, {"start": 189.0, "text": "On the signing and capability"}, {"start": 190.0, "text": "section, click Add Capability"}, {"start": 193.0, "text": "and select Background Modes."}, {"start": 196.0, "text": "Finally, under Background Modes,"}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "select the Audio Mode."}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "This is all that needs to be"}, {"start": 201.0, "text": "done. Now that the project is"}, {"start": 204.0, "text": "configured, let's talk about the"}, {"start": 206.0, "text": "different APIs that need to be"}, {"start": 208.0, "text": "used during audio playback."}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "After your app launches and"}, {"start": 212.0, "text": "before you activate an audio"}, {"start": 213.0, "text": "session, you may need to"}, {"start": 215.0, "text": "retrieve data from your servers."}, {"start": 218.0, "text": "This data is needed to present"}, {"start": 220.0, "text": "streaming options and content to"}, {"start": 222.0, "text": "users."}, {"start": 223.0, "text": "For example, album information,"}, {"start": 225.0, "text": "playlist information, all"}, {"start": 227.0, "text": "metadata about the content of"}, {"start": 228.0, "text": "your applicant stream."}, {"start": 230.0, "text": "You may have already cached this"}, {"start": 232.0, "text": "data when your app activated or"}, {"start": 234.0, "text": "during the background refresh"}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "opportunity."}, {"start": 236.0, "text": "If not, use URLSession to"}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "retrieve your data."}, {"start": 239.0, "text": "At this time, socket, streaming"}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "task, and the network framework"}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "will not be available for use."}, {"start": 247.0, "text": "Once you have all the"}, {"start": 248.0, "text": "information you need to begin"}, {"start": 249.0, "text": "streaming, activate an audio"}, {"start": 251.0, "text": "session."}, {"start": 252.0, "text": "The audio session should not be"}, {"start": 254.0, "text": "activated before this point,"}, {"start": 256.0, "text": "because activating one can"}, {"start": 258.0, "text": "disrupt the user experience."}, {"start": 260.0, "text": "This is a very important"}, {"start": 261.0, "text": "difference between watchOS and"}, {"start": 263.0, "text": "iOS. On iOS, there's always a default"}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "audio route available."}, {"start": 267.0, "text": "Let's figure out."}, {"start": 268.0, "text": "This is not the case for"}, {"start": 269.0, "text": "watchOS."}, {"start": 271.0, "text": "When you activate an audio"}, {"start": 272.0, "text": "session, watchOS will"}, {"start": 274.0, "text": "automatically present an audio"}, {"start": 275.0, "text": "route picker on behalf of your"}, {"start": 277.0, "text": "application if no route is"}, {"start": 279.0, "text": "currently active."}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "There are two cases where"}, {"start": 282.0, "text": "watchOS may be able to skip"}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "presenting the audio route"}, {"start": 285.0, "text": "picker."}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "For any Bluetooth device, if the"}, {"start": 288.0, "text": "device is already connected to"}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "the watch, or for Bluetooth"}, {"start": 292.0, "text": "devices based on the Apple"}, {"start": 294.0, "text": "wireless chip set, if the device"}, {"start": 296.0, "text": "is connected to the iPhone, the"}, {"start": 298.0, "text": "watch may temporarily borrow it."}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "There are cases where this is"}, {"start": 301.0, "text": "not possible though, for"}, {"start": 303.0, "text": "instance, if you are on a phone"}, {"start": 305.0, "text": "call while connected to your"}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "iPhone."}, {"start": 307.0, "text": "Once your application has an"}, {"start": 309.0, "text": "active audio session, all of the"}, {"start": 311.0, "text": "networking APIs are available to"}, {"start": 313.0, "text": "retrieve audio content."}, {"start": 315.0, "text": "This includes"}, {"start": 316.0, "text": "URLSessionStreamingTask,"}, {"start": 318.0, "text": "URLSessionWebSocketTask, and the"}, {"start": 320.0, "text": "network framework."}, {"start": 322.0, "text": "If you attempt to use these APIs"}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "without an active audio session,"}, {"start": 326.0, "text": "your calls will fail."}, {"start": 329.0, "text": "Finally, your application has"}, {"start": 331.0, "text": "reached the point where it has"}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "enough audio data to start"}, {"start": 333.0, "text": "playback."}, {"start": 334.0, "text": "You can now use AVFoundation to"}, {"start": 336.0, "text": "play your audio content."}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "If you need to request new information from your servers to"}, {"start": 342.0, "text": "do your streaming, you can use"}, {"start": 343.0, "text": "all available networking APIs to"}, {"start": 346.0, "text": "do this."}, {"start": 348.0, "text": "Now, let's talk about some audio"}, {"start": 349.0, "text": "streaming best practices for"}, {"start": 351.0, "text": "Apple Watch."}, {"start": 354.0, "text": "Audio streaming on Apple Watch"}, {"start": 355.0, "text": "is available in Series 3 and"}, {"start": 357.0, "text": "later."}, {"start": 358.0, "text": "This means that your application"}, {"start": 360.0, "text": "needs to check if audio"}, {"start": 361.0, "text": "streaming is available on the"}, {"start": 362.0, "text": "watch it is running on."}, {"start": 364.0, "text": "In watchOS 6, use"}, {"start": 365.0, "text": "WKInterphaseDevices"}, {"start": 368.0, "text": "supportsAudioStreaming to make"}, {"start": 370.0, "text": "this check."}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "The additional audio and"}, {"start": 373.0, "text": "networking APIs in watchOS 6"}, {"start": 376.0, "text": "mean that applications no longer"}, {"start": 378.0, "text": "need to use WatchKit's WK audio"}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "file APIs."}, {"start": 382.0, "text": "For this reason, these APIs have"}, {"start": 383.0, "text": "been deprecated starting with"}, {"start": 385.0, "text": "watchOS 6."}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "Now, let's discuss some"}, {"start": 388.0, "text": "networking best practices."}, {"start": 392.0, "text": "Caching is very important."}, {"start": 394.0, "text": "The right amount of audio data"}, {"start": 395.0, "text": "should be locally available at"}, {"start": 397.0, "text": "all times to cope with changing"}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "network conditions."}, {"start": 401.0, "text": "The number of network requests"}, {"start": 404.0, "text": "and their sizes should be"}, {"start": 405.0, "text": "reduced to the absolute minimum."}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "Extra requests that did not post"}, {"start": 409.0, "text": "a problem on other devices may"}, {"start": 411.0, "text": "delay or stall playback."}, {"start": 413.0, "text": "The same is true for downloading"}, {"start": 414.0, "text": "unnecessary data in those"}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "requests."}, {"start": 416.0, "text": "All of these can result in poor"}, {"start": 418.0, "text": "user experiences."}, {"start": 421.0, "text": "To be safe, start streaming"}, {"start": 423.0, "text": "using 64 kbps encoded audio"}, {"start": 426.0, "text": "data."}, {"start": 427.0, "text": "Monitor the speed at which data"}, {"start": 429.0, "text": "arrives to your application and"}, {"start": 431.0, "text": "only upgrade to higher bit rates"}, {"start": 433.0, "text": "if the network conditions allow"}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "for them."}, {"start": 435.0, "text": "AVFoundation automatically does"}, {"start": 437.0, "text": "this for HLS audio streaming."}, {"start": 441.0, "text": "Do not rely on network"}, {"start": 442.0, "text": "reachability."}, {"start": 443.0, "text": "Due to the nature of networks,"}, {"start": 445.0, "text": "the information returned by this"}, {"start": 447.0, "text": "API may no longer be valid by"}, {"start": 449.0, "text": "the time your application uses"}, {"start": 451.0, "text": "it. For the best user experience,"}, {"start": 454.0, "text": "always assume that you have a"}, {"start": 455.0, "text": "network connection and"}, {"start": 456.0, "text": "gracefully handle stalls and"}, {"start": 458.0, "text": "failures, and always adjust in"}, {"start": 461.0, "text": "real-time the audio quality and"}, {"start": 463.0, "text": "the amount of caching that your"}, {"start": 464.0, "text": "application does."}, {"start": 467.0, "text": "Finally, your application is"}, {"start": 469.0, "text": "likely to experience more"}, {"start": 470.0, "text": "network transitions when running"}, {"start": 471.0, "text": "an Apple Watch."}, {"start": 472.0, "text": "As the watch moves away from the"}, {"start": 474.0, "text": "iPhone, a good transition from"}, {"start": 476.0, "text": "Bluetooth to Wi-Fi or cellular."}, {"start": 478.0, "text": "It is not uncommon for the watch"}, {"start": 480.0, "text": "to go between these three"}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "network types while your app is"}, {"start": 482.0, "text": "running."}, {"start": 483.0, "text": "Your application should be"}, {"start": 484.0, "text": "prepared for such transitions,"}, {"start": 486.0, "text": "which can take several seconds"}, {"start": 488.0, "text": "to complete."}, {"start": 489.0, "text": "As you can see, when bringing"}, {"start": 491.0, "text": "audio streaming applications to"}, {"start": 492.0, "text": "Apple Watch from other"}, {"start": 493.0, "text": "platforms, Apple or otherwise,"}, {"start": 496.0, "text": "you should be prepared for the"}, {"start": 497.0, "text": "possibility that you will need"}, {"start": 498.0, "text": "to optimize your networking code"}, {"start": 500.0, "text": "and protocols."}, {"start": 501.0, "text": "If you need more information to"}, {"start": 503.0, "text": "get started writing audio"}, {"start": 505.0, "text": "applications for Apple Watch,"}, {"start": 507.0, "text": "Creating Audio Apps for watchOS"}, {"start": 509.0, "text": "is a great start."}, {"start": 510.0, "text": "The information in the network"}, {"start": 512.0, "text": "framework introduction talk is"}, {"start": 514.0, "text": "100% applicable to watchOS."}, {"start": 517.0, "text": "Finally, check out these other"}, {"start": 518.0, "text": "sessions to help create a great"}]}